// =====================================================================
// i18n.js · Page translation (Spanish / English)
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------
// i18n = "internationalization" (i + 18 letters + n).
//
// HOW IT WORKS
//   1. TEXTS: one dictionary per language (like a Python dict):
//      key → text. The keys are those of the HTML data-i18n
//      attributes, plus those of the texts generated by app.js.
//   2. aplicarIdioma(): walks the HTML and replaces each marked text.
//   3. When finished, it fires the "idioma-cambiado" event so that
//      app.js repaints what it generates itself (status, figures…).
//
// MAP
//   A. Language configuration
//   B. Text dictionary
//   C. Public functions: t() and locale() (used by app.js)
//   D. Apply a language to the page
//   E. Initial language and flag buttons
// =====================================================================


// ---------------------------------------------------------------------
// A. LANGUAGE CONFIGURATION
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------
